Package: homelab-notes
Architecture: all
Depends: perl (>= 5.36),
         homelab-common (>= 0.1.37),
         homelab-webtheme,
         libmojolicious-perl,
         libyaml-libyaml-perl,
         libmojo-pg-perl,
         adduser,
         curl,
         sudo
Recommends: homelab-api, homelab-sso, homelab-webproxy, homelab-audit, homelab-agent
Description: Notes web app for the homelab-* ecosystem
 notes.<domain>: notebooks (the tabs), folders, and notes written in
 Markdown, HTML or plain text and shown rendered; versions kept; links on a
 note to an email or a drive file; sharing to other accounts (see, or see
 and edit) or by link to anyone; search. Everything homelab-cli needs is
 behind homelab-api's /api/v1/notes/* gateway.
 .
 A BFF-style Mojolicious app like homelab-calendar: browsers talk only to
 this app; sign-in is delegated to homelab-sso and the token is held in
 this app's own session cookie, re-verified against homelab-api on every
 request. Data lives in its own `notes` Postgres schema (split
 runtime/migrate roles). Markdown is rendered and every HTML body is
 cleaned by the package's own pure-Perl code; nothing is loaded from a CDN.
